{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"heading","depth":1,"id":"code-weight-rename-private-members-in-the-tanstack-db-build","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Code weight: rename private members in the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/db"},{"type":"text","value":" build"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Reviewed executable revision: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"9c422842"},{"type":"text","value":" (base "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"c0d123b8"},{"type":"text","value":", the fetched\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"origin/main"},{"type":"text","value":" at review time). This record follows in a documentation-only\ncommit. The rename landed in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"6dbf3982"},{"type":"text","value":" on base "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"9125dab6"},{"type":"text","value":". Later commits fix\ntwo review findings, merge "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"origin/main"},{"type":"text","value":", and add the dist smoke lane."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"change","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Change"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Consumer minifiers rename local variables but never rename properties. Long\nTypeScript-private member names, such as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"authoritativeRequestState"},{"type":"text","value":" or\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"truncateReplayState"},{"type":"text","value":", therefore reach every production bundle in full. The\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/db"},{"type":"text","value":" build now renames 368 of those members to short names. The\nrenaming happens in a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"renderChunk"},{"type":"text","value":" step of "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"packages/db/vite.config.ts"},{"type":"text","value":", which\nruns esbuild "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"mangleProps"},{"type":"text","value":" on each emitted ESM and CJS module."}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"packages/db/mangle-cache.json"},{"type":"text","value":" is the committed map from each original\nname to its short name. It makes the renaming reversible and keeps the short\nnames stable across releases."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The build step fails if esbuild renames any name that is not in the cache."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"scripts/mangle-private-members.mjs"},{"type":"text","value":" checks the cache ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"pnpm check:mangle"},{"type":"text","value":")\nand updates it ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"--write"},{"type":"text","value":"). "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"--write"},{"type":"text","value":" keeps existing assignments, drops names\nthat are no longer safe, and gives new safe names the next free short names."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"scripts/test-minified-db.mjs"},{"type":"text","value":" now bundles the built "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"dist"},{"type":"text","value":", not "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"src"},{"type":"text","value":", and\nrejects a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"dist"},{"type":"text","value":" that is older than "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"src"},{"type":"text","value":", the cache, or the package's build\nconfiguration ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"vite.config.ts"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"package.json"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tsconfig.json"},{"type":"text","value":"). CI builds db-ivm and\ndb before this lane and runs "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"check:mangle"},{"type":"text","value":" first."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The published declarations, the public API, and the source maps do not\nchange. Each source map still points at the original TypeScript, which the\npackage also publishes in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"src"},{"type":"text","value":". "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/db-ivm"},{"type":"text","value":" is not renamed: it already\nuses native "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"#private"},{"type":"text","value":" members, and a probe showed a gain under 0.5% gzip."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"bytes","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Bytes"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Each row bundles the built "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"dist"},{"type":"text","value":" as a consumer would, with esbuild at target\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"es2020"},{"type":"text","value":", and both builds sit under the same "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"package.json"},{"type":"text","value":", so both apply\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"\"sideEffects\": false"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,"right","right","right"],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Consumer entry"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"min"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"gzip"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"brotli"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"full public API"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"−30,083 (−8.0%)"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"−2,917 (−2.7%)"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"−2,077 (−2.3%)"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"local-only collection with one insert"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"−10,951 (−8.4%)"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"−1,059 (−3.0%)"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"−718 (−2.3%)"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"collection with a filtered live query"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"−20,606 (−7.3%)"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"−1,901 (−2.4%)"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"−1,431 (−2.1%)"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"full public API, minified with terser"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"−30,074 (−7.9%)"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"−2,886 (−2.8%)"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"−1,869 (−2.2%)"}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The minified saving is large because each long name repeats in every bundle.\nGzip and brotli already encode most repeats as short back-references, so the\ncompressed saving is smaller."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"An earlier measurement of the minimal entry showed a gzip saving of 13%. That\nwas a harness fault: the unrenamed copy sat outside the package, so esbuild did\nnot apply "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"\"sideEffects\": false"},{"type":"text","value":" to it and kept nine modules that have\ntop-level registration statements. With both builds under the same\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"package.json"},{"type":"text","value":", the minimal entry saves 2.9% gzip."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"why-the-rename-is-safe","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Why the rename is safe"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"esbuild renames every property with a cached name, anywhere in the output,\nwithout regard to types. So "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"map.size"},{"type":"text","value":" on a native "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Map"},{"type":"text","value":" would also change if\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"size"},{"type":"text","value":" were a cached name. The safety rule therefore covers every use of each\nname, not only the uses on the private member."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A name is safe when all of these hold:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"start":1,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Every property-name use of it in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"packages/db/src"},{"type":"text","value":" resolves, through the\nTypeScript checker, to a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"private"},{"type":"text","value":" class member declared in\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"packages/db/src"},{"type":"text","value":". The uses include property access, object literal keys,\nclass members, constructor parameter properties, interface members,\ndestructuring, and shorthand properties.\nAn unresolved use (an "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"any"},{"type":"text","value":" receiver) or a use that resolves to another\ndeclaration (a lib type, db-ivm, an internal interface) makes the name\nunsafe."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"It never appears as a string literal in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"packages/db/src"},{"type":"text","value":". esbuild does not\nrename quoted keys."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"No other package's "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"src"},{"type":"text","value":" or tests read "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":".name"},{"type":"text","value":" or a quoted "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'name'"},{"type":"text","value":". Those\npackages consume the renamed "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"dist"},{"type":"text","value":", so an untyped read would break."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Each short name must also be unique and must not be an identifier anywhere in\ndb or db-ivm "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"src"},{"type":"text","value":", so a renamed member cannot collide with a real property."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Of 470 private member names, 368 pass. The first text-based probe for this\nchange used public "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":".d.ts"},{"type":"text","value":" output as a fourth filter. Every name that filter\nalone removed appeared in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":".d.ts"},{"type":"text","value":" only in a comment, in a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"private"},{"type":"text","value":"\ndeclaration, or as a function or constructor parameter name. None of those is\na property. The type-checked rule covers public\ntypes directly, because a name in a public type has a non-private declaration."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"guard-calibration","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Guard calibration"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Each row plants one hostile use of the cached name "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"authoritativeRequestState"},{"type":"text","value":"\n(short name "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"l"},{"type":"text","value":") and runs "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"pnpm check:mangle"},{"type":"text","value":". Every row exits with status 1\nand names the file and line."}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Planted use"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Guard result"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"C1: public object literal key in db src"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"PropertyAssignment ... used at src/SortedMap.ts"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"C2: untyped read "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"(globalThis as any).name"},{"type":"text","value":" in db src"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"unresolved use"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"C3: string literal of the name in db src"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string literal"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"C4: untyped read in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"packages/react-db/src"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"used in packages/react-db/src/index.ts"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"C5: an identifier equal to the short name "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"l"},{"type":"text","value":" in db src"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"l is an identifier in src"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"C6: an interface member with the same name"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"PropertySignature ... used at src/SortedMap.ts"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"C7: a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"public"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"readonly"},{"type":"text","value":", or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"protected"},{"type":"text","value":" constructor parameter property"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Parameter in packages/db/src/SortedMap.ts"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Control: a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"private"},{"type":"text","value":" constructor parameter property"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"passes (status 0)"}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"CodeRabbit review of "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"3799ffa4"},{"type":"text","value":" found that the first guard never visited\nconstructor parameters. A non-private parameter property with a cached name\npassed the check in all three modifier forms. The guard now checks every\nparameter property as a property declaration. No current source had such a\nproperty, so the cache did not change."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The minified lane keeps its three hostile controls. With the lane bundling\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"dist"},{"type":"text","value":", the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"new.target.name"},{"type":"text","value":" control first passed silently, because its mutant\nplugin matched "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"src/errors.ts"},{"type":"text","value":", which the bundle no longer loads. The plugin\nnow matches "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"dist/esm/errors.js"},{"type":"text","value":", and all three controls fail at their intended\nassertions:"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Control"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Result"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"--calibrate-error-name"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"assertion failure: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"CollectionConfigurationError.name"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"--calibrate-public-member"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"assertion failure: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"public index metadata method"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"--calibrate-output-shape"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"assertion failure: query rows differ"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"a source file newer than "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"dist"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"error: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"packages/db/dist is older than packages/db/src/SortedMap.ts"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"vite.config.ts"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"package.json"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tsconfig.json"},{"type":"text","value":", or the cache newer than "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"dist"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"error naming that file"}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"An external review of "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"a1d2b85b"},{"type":"text","value":" found that the freshness check did not\ninclude the build configuration. With only "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"vite.config.ts"},{"type":"text","value":" touched after a\nbuild, the lane passed against output from the older pipeline. The check now\nincludes the configuration files. Each input was touched alone after a fresh\nbuild, and each one fails the check with its own path."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"behavior-evidence","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Behavior evidence"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The rename changes no source, so the db suite, which runs against "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"src"},{"type":"text","value":",\ncannot observe it. Every package that depends on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/db"},{"type":"text","value":" resolves it\nthrough the workspace to the built "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"dist"},{"type":"text","value":", so their suites run against the\nrenamed output. On "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"6dbf3982"},{"type":"text","value":", with the 368-name cache:"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,"right","right"],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Package"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Files"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Tests"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/angular-db"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"2"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"57 passed, 1 todo"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/db-sqlite-persistence-core"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"9"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"369 passed, 1 todo"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/electric-db-collection"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"13"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"585"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/offline-transactions"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"17"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"202"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/powersync-db-collection"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"9"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"173"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/query-db-collection"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"15"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"532"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/react-db"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"13"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"286"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/rxdb-db-collection"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"1"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"12"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/solid-db"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"2"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"81"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/svelte-db"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"6"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"107"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/trailbase-db-collection"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"3"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"67"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/vue-db"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"5"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"109"}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"These 2,580 tests pass. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"test:minified-db"},{"type":"text","value":" also passes against the renamed\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"dist"},{"type":"text","value":". The run used the working tree just before "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"6dbf3982"},{"type":"text","value":". That commit\nchanges only formatting and one lint fix in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"vite.config.ts"},{"type":"text","value":", and its built\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"dist"},{"type":"text","value":" is byte-identical to the verified build. After the merge of\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"origin/main"},{"type":"text","value":" at "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"7b8142fc"},{"type":"text","value":", CI's Test job ran every consumer suite against\nthe rebuilt, renamed "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"dist"},{"type":"text","value":" and passed."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"db-tests-against-the-renamed-dist","children":[{"type":"text","value":"db tests against the renamed dist"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The consumer suites reach db only through other packages. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"pnpm --filter @tanstack/db test:dist"},{"type":"text","value":" also runs five of db's own test files against the\nbuilt "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"dist"},{"type":"text","value":". "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"packages/db/vitest.dist.config.ts"},{"type":"text","value":" maps each "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"src"},{"type":"text","value":" import to the\nmatching built module, which exists because the build emits one module per\nsource module. Modules without runtime code (re-export barrels and type-only\nfiles) are not emitted, so those load from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"src"},{"type":"text","value":", and their imports then\nresolve to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"dist"},{"type":"text","value":". Any other unbuilt module throws. A planted "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"throw"},{"type":"text","value":" in the\nbuilt "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"collection/index.js"},{"type":"text","value":" showed that the lane loads "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"dist"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The five files were chosen for coverage of the 14 modules that hold about 90%\nof the renamed members. Coverage is measured on the built modules and mapped\nback to source. Files that read renamed members directly were excluded,\nbecause they would test the rename map instead of behavior."}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,"right","right"],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"File"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"New key-module statements"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Cumulative"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"query/ordered-source-loader-state.test.ts"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"1,951"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"37.4%"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"live-query-observer.test.ts"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"641"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"49.8%"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"query/includes-publication-oracle.test.ts"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"479"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"58.9%"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"query/bucket-facade-adapter.test.ts"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"178"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"62.4%"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"collection-subscription.test.ts"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"179"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"65.8%"}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The five files run 254 tests in about 3 seconds. All 14 measured candidates\ntogether reached only 72.6%. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"live-query-window-controller"},{"type":"text","value":" has no coverage\nfrom db tests that avoid its internals. The framework adapters' infinite-query\nsuites exercise it, and they run against "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"dist"},{"type":"text","value":" in CI's Test job."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Calibration: in the built "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ordered-source-loader.js"},{"type":"text","value":", the first of 26 "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":".l"},{"type":"text","value":"\naccesses was restored to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":".authoritativeRequestState"},{"type":"text","value":", which is an inconsistent\nrename. The lane then failed 48 of 254 tests in 2 of 5 files. With the file\nrestored, all 254 tests pass. A source file newer than "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"dist"},{"type":"text","value":" makes the lane\nthrow the freshness error before any test runs."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"costs","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Costs"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"dist"},{"type":"text","value":" JavaScript is harder to read directly ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"this.ay"},{"type":"text","value":"). Source maps and the\ncache decode it. Stack traces that are not source-mapped show short method\nnames for renamed private methods."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"esbuild reprints each emitted module. The reprint keeps "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@__PURE__"},{"type":"text","value":"\nannotations (299 before and after) and legal comments, and drops other\nJavaScript comments. The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":".d.ts"},{"type":"text","value":" documentation does not change."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The db build takes about one second longer."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"limits","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Limits"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The rule is static. Reflection that enumerates instance properties (for\nexample "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Object.keys(collection)"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"JSON.stringify"},{"type":"text","value":" of a class instance)\nwould see short names. No such use exists in the checked packages, and the\nconsumer suites pass, but a user who inspects internal instances this way\nwould see different keys."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A private member added later is not renamed until someone runs "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"--write"},{"type":"text","value":".\nThat costs bytes but is never unsafe."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"check:mangle"},{"type":"text","value":" reads other packages in this repository only. Code outside\nthe repository that reads "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/db"},{"type":"text","value":" internals through "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"any"},{"type":"text","value":" is\nunsupported and can break."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"verification","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Verification"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"On "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"9c422842"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"pnpm check:mangle"},{"type":"text","value":": 368 names."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"pnpm --filter @tanstack/db test:dist"},{"type":"text","value":": 5 files, 254 tests."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"pnpm test:minified-db"},{"type":"text","value":" against the built "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"dist"},{"type":"text","value":": error names, index\nmetadata, query rows, and live updates."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"packages/db"},{"type":"text","value":" Vitest, typecheck off: 193 files, 7,164 tests."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"pnpm test:oracles"},{"type":"text","value":": 49 "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/db"},{"type":"text","value":" files with 2,847 tests, and 16\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/query-db-collection"},{"type":"text","value":" files with 454 tests and 1 todo."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The consumer suites in the table above ran on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"6dbf3982"},{"type":"text","value":". On "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"7b8142fc"},{"type":"text","value":",\nCI's Test job ran them again against the merged, renamed "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"dist"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The environment was Node "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"v24.19.0"},{"type":"text","value":" and Vitest "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"3.2.4"},{"type":"text","value":" on Darwin arm64."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"code-weight-rename-private-members-in-the-tanstack-db-build","text":"Code weight: rename private members in the @tanstack/db build","level":1},{"id":"change","text":"Change","level":2},{"id":"bytes","text":"Bytes","level":2},{"id":"why-the-rename-is-safe","text":"Why the rename is safe","level":2},{"id":"guard-calibration","text":"Guard calibration","level":2},{"id":"behavior-evidence","text":"Behavior evidence","level":2},{"id":"db-tests-against-the-renamed-dist","text":"db tests against the renamed dist","level":3},{"id":"costs","text":"Costs","level":2},{"id":"limits","text":"Limits","level":2},{"id":"verification","text":"Verification","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"# Code weight: rename private members in the `@tanstack/db` build\n\nReviewed executable revision: `9c422842` (base `c0d123b8`, the fetched\n`origin/main` at review time). This record follows in a documentation-only\ncommit. The rename landed in `6dbf3982` on base `9125dab6`. Later commits fix\ntwo review findings, merge `origin/main`, and add the dist smoke lane.\n\n## Change\n\nConsumer minifiers rename local variables but never rename properties. Long\nTypeScript-private member names, such as `authoritativeRequestState` or\n`truncateReplayState`, therefore reach every production bundle in full. The\n`@tanstack/db` build now renames 368 of those members to short names. The\nrenaming happens in a `renderChunk` step of `packages/db/vite.config.ts`, which\nruns esbuild `mangleProps` on each emitted ESM and CJS module.\n\n- `packages/db/mangle-cache.json` is the committed map from each original\n  name to its short name. It makes the renaming reversible and keeps the short\n  names stable across releases.\n- The build step fails if esbuild renames any name that is not in the cache.\n- `scripts/mangle-private-members.mjs` checks the cache (`pnpm check:mangle`)\n  and updates it (`--write`). `--write` keeps existing assignments, drops names\n  that are no longer safe, and gives new safe names the next free short names.\n- `scripts/test-minified-db.mjs` now bundles the built `dist`, not `src`, and\n  rejects a `dist` that is older than `src`, the cache, or the package's build\n  configuration (`vite.config.ts`, `package.json`, `tsconfig.json`). CI builds db-ivm and\n  db before this lane and runs `check:mangle` first.\n\nThe published declarations, the public API, and the source maps do not\nchange. Each source map still points at the original TypeScript, which the\npackage also publishes in `src`. `@tanstack/db-ivm` is not renamed: it already\nuses native `#private` members, and a probe showed a gain under 0.5% gzip.\n\n## Bytes\n\nEach row bundles the built `dist` as a consumer would, with esbuild at target\n`es2020`, and both builds sit under the same `package.json`, so both apply\n`\"sideEffects\": false`.\n\n| Consumer entry | min | gzip | brotli |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| full public API | −30,083 (−8.0%) | −2,917 (−2.7%) | −2,077 (−2.3%) |\n| local-only collection with one insert | −10,951 (−8.4%) | −1,059 (−3.0%) | −718 (−2.3%) |\n| collection with a filtered live query | −20,606 (−7.3%) | −1,901 (−2.4%) | −1,431 (−2.1%) |\n| full public API, minified with terser | −30,074 (−7.9%) | −2,886 (−2.8%) | −1,869 (−2.2%) |\n\nThe minified saving is large because each long name repeats in every bundle.\nGzip and brotli already encode most repeats as short back-references, so the\ncompressed saving is smaller.\n\nAn earlier measurement of the minimal entry showed a gzip saving of 13%. That\nwas a harness fault: the unrenamed copy sat outside the package, so esbuild did\nnot apply `\"sideEffects\": false` to it and kept nine modules that have\ntop-level registration statements. With both builds under the same\n`package.json`, the minimal entry saves 2.9% gzip.\n\n## Why the rename is safe\n\nesbuild renames every property with a cached name, anywhere in the output,\nwithout regard to types. So `map.size` on a native `Map` would also change if\n`size` were a cached name. The safety rule therefore covers every use of each\nname, not only the uses on the private member.\n\nA name is safe when all of these hold:\n\n1. Every property-name use of it in `packages/db/src` resolves, through the\n   TypeScript checker, to a `private` class member declared in\n   `packages/db/src`. The uses include property access, object literal keys,\n   class members, constructor parameter properties, interface members,\n   destructuring, and shorthand properties.\n   An unresolved use (an `any` receiver) or a use that resolves to another\n   declaration (a lib type, db-ivm, an internal interface) makes the name\n   unsafe.\n2. It never appears as a string literal in `packages/db/src`. esbuild does not\n   rename quoted keys.\n3. No other package's `src` or tests read `.name` or a quoted `'name'`. Those\n   packages consume the renamed `dist`, so an untyped read would break.\n\nEach short name must also be unique and must not be an identifier anywhere in\ndb or db-ivm `src`, so a renamed member cannot collide with a real property.\n\nOf 470 private member names, 368 pass. The first text-based probe for this\nchange used public `.d.ts` output as a fourth filter. Every name that filter\nalone removed appeared in `.d.ts` only in a comment, in a `private`\ndeclaration, or as a function or constructor parameter name. None of those is\na property. The type-checked rule covers public\ntypes directly, because a name in a public type has a non-private declaration.\n\n## Guard calibration\n\nEach row plants one hostile use of the cached name `authoritativeRequestState`\n(short name `l`) and runs `pnpm check:mangle`. Every row exits with status 1\nand names the file and line.\n\n| Planted use | Guard result |\n| --- | --- |\n| C1: public object literal key in db src | `PropertyAssignment ... used at src/SortedMap.ts` |\n| C2: untyped read `(globalThis as any).name` in db src | `unresolved use` |\n| C3: string literal of the name in db src | `string literal` |\n| C4: untyped read in `packages/react-db/src` | `used in packages/react-db/src/index.ts` |\n| C5: an identifier equal to the short name `l` in db src | `l is an identifier in src` |\n| C6: an interface member with the same name | `PropertySignature ... used at src/SortedMap.ts` |\n| C7: a `public`, `readonly`, or `protected` constructor parameter property | `Parameter in packages/db/src/SortedMap.ts` |\n| Control: a `private` constructor parameter property | passes (status 0) |\n\nCodeRabbit review of `3799ffa4` found that the first guard never visited\nconstructor parameters. A non-private parameter property with a cached name\npassed the check in all three modifier forms. The guard now checks every\nparameter property as a property declaration. No current source had such a\nproperty, so the cache did not change.\n\nThe minified lane keeps its three hostile controls. With the lane bundling\n`dist`, the `new.target.name` control first passed silently, because its mutant\nplugin matched `src/errors.ts`, which the bundle no longer loads. The plugin\nnow matches `dist/esm/errors.js`, and all three controls fail at their intended\nassertions:\n\n| Control | Result |\n| --- | --- |\n| `--calibrate-error-name` | assertion failure: `CollectionConfigurationError.name` |\n| `--calibrate-public-member` | assertion failure: `public index metadata method` |\n| `--calibrate-output-shape` | assertion failure: query rows differ |\n| a source file newer than `dist` | error: `packages/db/dist is older than packages/db/src/SortedMap.ts` |\n| `vite.config.ts`, `package.json`, `tsconfig.json`, or the cache newer than `dist` | error naming that file |\n\nAn external review of `a1d2b85b` found that the freshness check did not\ninclude the build configuration. With only `vite.config.ts` touched after a\nbuild, the lane passed against output from the older pipeline. The check now\nincludes the configuration files. Each input was touched alone after a fresh\nbuild, and each one fails the check with its own path.\n\n## Behavior evidence\n\nThe rename changes no source, so the db suite, which runs against `src`,\ncannot observe it. Every package that depends on `@tanstack/db` resolves it\nthrough the workspace to the built `dist`, so their suites run against the\nrenamed output. On `6dbf3982`, with the 368-name cache:\n\n| Package | Files | Tests |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| `@tanstack/angular-db` | 2 | 57 passed, 1 todo |\n| `@tanstack/db-sqlite-persistence-core` | 9 | 369 passed, 1 todo |\n| `@tanstack/electric-db-collection` | 13 | 585 |\n| `@tanstack/offline-transactions` | 17 | 202 |\n| `@tanstack/powersync-db-collection` | 9 | 173 |\n| `@tanstack/query-db-collection` | 15 | 532 |\n| `@tanstack/react-db` | 13 | 286 |\n| `@tanstack/rxdb-db-collection` | 1 | 12 |\n| `@tanstack/solid-db` | 2 | 81 |\n| `@tanstack/svelte-db` | 6 | 107 |\n| `@tanstack/trailbase-db-collection` | 3 | 67 |\n| `@tanstack/vue-db` | 5 | 109 |\n\nThese 2,580 tests pass. `test:minified-db` also passes against the renamed\n`dist`. The run used the working tree just before `6dbf3982`. That commit\nchanges only formatting and one lint fix in `vite.config.ts`, and its built\n`dist` is byte-identical to the verified build. After the merge of\n`origin/main` at `7b8142fc`, CI's Test job ran every consumer suite against\nthe rebuilt, renamed `dist` and passed.\n\n### db tests against the renamed dist\n\nThe consumer suites reach db only through other packages. `pnpm --filter\n@tanstack/db test:dist` also runs five of db's own test files against the\nbuilt `dist`. `packages/db/vitest.dist.config.ts` maps each `src` import to the\nmatching built module, which exists because the build emits one module per\nsource module. Modules without runtime code (re-export barrels and type-only\nfiles) are not emitted, so those load from `src`, and their imports then\nresolve to `dist`. Any other unbuilt module throws. A planted `throw` in the\nbuilt `collection/index.js` showed that the lane loads `dist`.\n\nThe five files were chosen for coverage of the 14 modules that hold about 90%\nof the renamed members. Coverage is measured on the built modules and mapped\nback to source. Files that read renamed members directly were excluded,\nbecause they would test the rename map instead of behavior.\n\n| File | New key-module statements | Cumulative |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| `query/ordered-source-loader-state.test.ts` | 1,951 | 37.4% |\n| `live-query-observer.test.ts` | 641 | 49.8% |\n| `query/includes-publication-oracle.test.ts` | 479 | 58.9% |\n| `query/bucket-facade-adapter.test.ts` | 178 | 62.4% |\n| `collection-subscription.test.ts` | 179 | 65.8% |\n\nThe five files run 254 tests in about 3 seconds. All 14 measured candidates\ntogether reached only 72.6%. `live-query-window-controller` has no coverage\nfrom db tests that avoid its internals. The framework adapters' infinite-query\nsuites exercise it, and they run against `dist` in CI's Test job.\n\nCalibration: in the built `ordered-source-loader.js`, the first of 26 `.l`\naccesses was restored to `.authoritativeRequestState`, which is an inconsistent\nrename. The lane then failed 48 of 254 tests in 2 of 5 files. With the file\nrestored, all 254 tests pass. A source file newer than `dist` makes the lane\nthrow the freshness error before any test runs.\n\n## Costs\n\n- `dist` JavaScript is harder to read directly (`this.ay`). Source maps and the\n  cache decode it. Stack traces that are not source-mapped show short method\n  names for renamed private methods.\n- esbuild reprints each emitted module. The reprint keeps `@__PURE__`\n  annotations (299 before and after) and legal comments, and drops other\n  JavaScript comments. The `.d.ts` documentation does not change.\n- The db build takes about one second longer.\n\n## Limits\n\n- The rule is static. Reflection that enumerates instance properties (for\n  example `Object.keys(collection)` or `JSON.stringify` of a class instance)\n  would see short names. No such use exists in the checked packages, and the\n  consumer suites pass, but a user who inspects internal instances this way\n  would see different keys.\n- A private member added later is not renamed until someone runs `--write`.\n  That costs bytes but is never unsafe.\n- `check:mangle` reads other packages in this repository only. Code outside\n  the repository that reads `@tanstack/db` internals through `any` is\n  unsupported and can break.\n\n## Verification\n\nOn `9c422842`:\n\n- `pnpm check:mangle`: 368 names.\n- `pnpm --filter @tanstack/db test:dist`: 5 files, 254 tests.\n- `pnpm test:minified-db` against the built `dist`: error names, index\n  metadata, query rows, and live updates.\n- `packages/db` Vitest, typecheck off: 193 files, 7,164 tests.\n- `pnpm test:oracles`: 49 `@tanstack/db` files with 2,847 tests, and 16\n  `@tanstack/query-db-collection` files with 454 tests and 1 todo.\n- The consumer suites in the table above ran on `6dbf3982`. On `7b8142fc`,\n  CI's Test job ran them again against the merged, renamed `dist`.\n\nThe environment was Node `v24.19.0` and Vitest `3.2.4` on Darwin arm64.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"# Code weight: rename private members in the `@tanstack/db` build\n\nReviewed executable revision: `9c422842` (base `c0d123b8`, the fetched\n`origin/main` at review time). This record follows in a documentation-only\ncommit. The rename landed in `6dbf3982` on base `9125dab6`. Later commits fix\ntwo review findings, merge `origin/main`, and add the dist smoke lane.\n\n## Change\n\nConsumer minifiers rename local variables but never rename properties. Long\nTypeScript-private member names, such as `authoritativeRequestState` or\n`truncateReplayState`, therefore reach every production bundle in full. The\n`@tanstack/db` build now renames 368 of those members to short names. The\nrenaming happens in a `renderChunk` step of `packages/db/vite.config.ts`, which\nruns esbuild `mangleProps` on each emitted ESM and CJS module.\n\n- `packages/db/mangle-cache.json` is the committed map from each original\n  name to its short name. It makes the renaming reversible and keeps the short\n  names stable across releases.\n- The build step fails if esbuild renames any name that is not in the cache.\n- `scripts/mangle-private-members.mjs` checks the cache (`pnpm check:mangle`)\n  and updates it (`--write`). `--write` keeps existing assignments, drops names\n  that are no longer safe, and gives new safe names the next free short names.\n- `scripts/test-minified-db.mjs` now bundles the built `dist`, not `src`, and\n  rejects a `dist` that is older than `src`, the cache, or the package's build\n  configuration (`vite.config.ts`, `package.json`, `tsconfig.json`). CI builds db-ivm and\n  db before this lane and runs `check:mangle` first.\n\nThe published declarations, the public API, and the source maps do not\nchange. Each source map still points at the original TypeScript, which the\npackage also publishes in `src`. `@tanstack/db-ivm` is not renamed: it already\nuses native `#private` members, and a probe showed a gain under 0.5% gzip.\n\n## Bytes\n\nEach row bundles the built `dist` as a consumer would, with esbuild at target\n`es2020`, and both builds sit under the same `package.json`, so both apply\n`\"sideEffects\": false`.\n\n| Consumer entry | min | gzip | brotli |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| full public API | −30,083 (−8.0%) | −2,917 (−2.7%) | −2,077 (−2.3%) |\n| local-only collection with one insert | −10,951 (−8.4%) | −1,059 (−3.0%) | −718 (−2.3%) |\n| collection with a filtered live query | −20,606 (−7.3%) | −1,901 (−2.4%) | −1,431 (−2.1%) |\n| full public API, minified with terser | −30,074 (−7.9%) | −2,886 (−2.8%) | −1,869 (−2.2%) |\n\nThe minified saving is large because each long name repeats in every bundle.\nGzip and brotli already encode most repeats as short back-references, so the\ncompressed saving is smaller.\n\nAn earlier measurement of the minimal entry showed a gzip saving of 13%. That\nwas a harness fault: the unrenamed copy sat outside the package, so esbuild did\nnot apply `\"sideEffects\": false` to it and kept nine modules that have\ntop-level registration statements. With both builds under the same\n`package.json`, the minimal entry saves 2.9% gzip.\n\n## Why the rename is safe\n\nesbuild renames every property with a cached name, anywhere in the output,\nwithout regard to types. So `map.size` on a native `Map` would also change if\n`size` were a cached name. The safety rule therefore covers every use of each\nname, not only the uses on the private member.\n\nA name is safe when all of these hold:\n\n1. Every property-name use of it in `packages/db/src` resolves, through the\n   TypeScript checker, to a `private` class member declared in\n   `packages/db/src`. The uses include property access, object literal keys,\n   class members, constructor parameter properties, interface members,\n   destructuring, and shorthand properties.\n   An unresolved use (an `any` receiver) or a use that resolves to another\n   declaration (a lib type, db-ivm, an internal interface) makes the name\n   unsafe.\n2. It never appears as a string literal in `packages/db/src`. esbuild does not\n   rename quoted keys.\n3. No other package's `src` or tests read `.name` or a quoted `'name'`. Those\n   packages consume the renamed `dist`, so an untyped read would break.\n\nEach short name must also be unique and must not be an identifier anywhere in\ndb or db-ivm `src`, so a renamed member cannot collide with a real property.\n\nOf 470 private member names, 368 pass. The first text-based probe for this\nchange used public `.d.ts` output as a fourth filter. Every name that filter\nalone removed appeared in `.d.ts` only in a comment, in a `private`\ndeclaration, or as a function or constructor parameter name. None of those is\na property. The type-checked rule covers public\ntypes directly, because a name in a public type has a non-private declaration.\n\n## Guard calibration\n\nEach row plants one hostile use of the cached name `authoritativeRequestState`\n(short name `l`) and runs `pnpm check:mangle`. Every row exits with status 1\nand names the file and line.\n\n| Planted use | Guard result |\n| --- | --- |\n| C1: public object literal key in db src | `PropertyAssignment ... used at src/SortedMap.ts` |\n| C2: untyped read `(globalThis as any).name` in db src | `unresolved use` |\n| C3: string literal of the name in db src | `string literal` |\n| C4: untyped read in `packages/react-db/src` | `used in packages/react-db/src/index.ts` |\n| C5: an identifier equal to the short name `l` in db src | `l is an identifier in src` |\n| C6: an interface member with the same name | `PropertySignature ... used at src/SortedMap.ts` |\n| C7: a `public`, `readonly`, or `protected` constructor parameter property | `Parameter in packages/db/src/SortedMap.ts` |\n| Control: a `private` constructor parameter property | passes (status 0) |\n\nCodeRabbit review of `3799ffa4` found that the first guard never visited\nconstructor parameters. A non-private parameter property with a cached name\npassed the check in all three modifier forms. The guard now checks every\nparameter property as a property declaration. No current source had such a\nproperty, so the cache did not change.\n\nThe minified lane keeps its three hostile controls. With the lane bundling\n`dist`, the `new.target.name` control first passed silently, because its mutant\nplugin matched `src/errors.ts`, which the bundle no longer loads. The plugin\nnow matches `dist/esm/errors.js`, and all three controls fail at their intended\nassertions:\n\n| Control | Result |\n| --- | --- |\n| `--calibrate-error-name` | assertion failure: `CollectionConfigurationError.name` |\n| `--calibrate-public-member` | assertion failure: `public index metadata method` |\n| `--calibrate-output-shape` | assertion failure: query rows differ |\n| a source file newer than `dist` | error: `packages/db/dist is older than packages/db/src/SortedMap.ts` |\n| `vite.config.ts`, `package.json`, `tsconfig.json`, or the cache newer than `dist` | error naming that file |\n\nAn external review of `a1d2b85b` found that the freshness check did not\ninclude the build configuration. With only `vite.config.ts` touched after a\nbuild, the lane passed against output from the older pipeline. The check now\nincludes the configuration files. Each input was touched alone after a fresh\nbuild, and each one fails the check with its own path.\n\n## Behavior evidence\n\nThe rename changes no source, so the db suite, which runs against `src`,\ncannot observe it. Every package that depends on `@tanstack/db` resolves it\nthrough the workspace to the built `dist`, so their suites run against the\nrenamed output. On `6dbf3982`, with the 368-name cache:\n\n| Package | Files | Tests |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| `@tanstack/angular-db` | 2 | 57 passed, 1 todo |\n| `@tanstack/db-sqlite-persistence-core` | 9 | 369 passed, 1 todo |\n| `@tanstack/electric-db-collection` | 13 | 585 |\n| `@tanstack/offline-transactions` | 17 | 202 |\n| `@tanstack/powersync-db-collection` | 9 | 173 |\n| `@tanstack/query-db-collection` | 15 | 532 |\n| `@tanstack/react-db` | 13 | 286 |\n| `@tanstack/rxdb-db-collection` | 1 | 12 |\n| `@tanstack/solid-db` | 2 | 81 |\n| `@tanstack/svelte-db` | 6 | 107 |\n| `@tanstack/trailbase-db-collection` | 3 | 67 |\n| `@tanstack/vue-db` | 5 | 109 |\n\nThese 2,580 tests pass. `test:minified-db` also passes against the renamed\n`dist`. The run used the working tree just before `6dbf3982`. That commit\nchanges only formatting and one lint fix in `vite.config.ts`, and its built\n`dist` is byte-identical to the verified build. After the merge of\n`origin/main` at `7b8142fc`, CI's Test job ran every consumer suite against\nthe rebuilt, renamed `dist` and passed.\n\n### db tests against the renamed dist\n\nThe consumer suites reach db only through other packages. `pnpm --filter\n@tanstack/db test:dist` also runs five of db's own test files against the\nbuilt `dist`. `packages/db/vitest.dist.config.ts` maps each `src` import to the\nmatching built module, which exists because the build emits one module per\nsource module. Modules without runtime code (re-export barrels and type-only\nfiles) are not emitted, so those load from `src`, and their imports then\nresolve to `dist`. Any other unbuilt module throws. A planted `throw` in the\nbuilt `collection/index.js` showed that the lane loads `dist`.\n\nThe five files were chosen for coverage of the 14 modules that hold about 90%\nof the renamed members. Coverage is measured on the built modules and mapped\nback to source. Files that read renamed members directly were excluded,\nbecause they would test the rename map instead of behavior.\n\n| File | New key-module statements | Cumulative |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| `query/ordered-source-loader-state.test.ts` | 1,951 | 37.4% |\n| `live-query-observer.test.ts` | 641 | 49.8% |\n| `query/includes-publication-oracle.test.ts` | 479 | 58.9% |\n| `query/bucket-facade-adapter.test.ts` | 178 | 62.4% |\n| `collection-subscription.test.ts` | 179 | 65.8% |\n\nThe five files run 254 tests in about 3 seconds. All 14 measured candidates\ntogether reached only 72.6%. `live-query-window-controller` has no coverage\nfrom db tests that avoid its internals. The framework adapters' infinite-query\nsuites exercise it, and they run against `dist` in CI's Test job.\n\nCalibration: in the built `ordered-source-loader.js`, the first of 26 `.l`\naccesses was restored to `.authoritativeRequestState`, which is an inconsistent\nrename. The lane then failed 48 of 254 tests in 2 of 5 files. With the file\nrestored, all 254 tests pass. A source file newer than `dist` makes the lane\nthrow the freshness error before any test runs.\n\n## Costs\n\n- `dist` JavaScript is harder to read directly (`this.ay`). Source maps and the\n  cache decode it. Stack traces that are not source-mapped show short method\n  names for renamed private methods.\n- esbuild reprints each emitted module. The reprint keeps `@__PURE__`\n  annotations (299 before and after) and legal comments, and drops other\n  JavaScript comments. The `.d.ts` documentation does not change.\n- The db build takes about one second longer.\n\n## Limits\n\n- The rule is static. Reflection that enumerates instance properties (for\n  example `Object.keys(collection)` or `JSON.stringify` of a class instance)\n  would see short names. No such use exists in the checked packages, and the\n  consumer suites pass, but a user who inspects internal instances this way\n  would see different keys.\n- A private member added later is not renamed until someone runs `--write`.\n  That costs bytes but is never unsafe.\n- `check:mangle` reads other packages in this repository only. Code outside\n  the repository that reads `@tanstack/db` internals through `any` is\n  unsupported and can break.\n\n## Verification\n\nOn `9c422842`:\n\n- `pnpm check:mangle`: 368 names.\n- `pnpm --filter @tanstack/db test:dist`: 5 files, 254 tests.\n- `pnpm test:minified-db` against the built `dist`: error names, index\n  metadata, query rows, and live updates.\n- `packages/db` Vitest, typecheck off: 193 files, 7,164 tests.\n- `pnpm test:oracles`: 49 `@tanstack/db` files with 2,847 tests, and 16\n  `@tanstack/query-db-collection` files with 454 tests and 1 todo.\n- The consumer suites in the table above ran on `6dbf3982`. On `7b8142fc`,\n  CI's Test job ran them again against the merged, renamed `dist`.\n\nThe environment was Node `v24.19.0` and Vitest `3.2.4` on Darwin arm64.\n"}
